# Kumaşgöz — Phase rules

## Product
Industrial textile anomaly detection on fabric production lines. Softwaresimulates-first; hardware comes after Phase 1.

## Active phase
Phase 1 — MVP live loop E2E done (blur → ensemble → actuation → SQLite).
Optional next: online GPU infer (not score-bank), camera capture stub, dashboard live tail.

## Phase 0 success
PatchCore (and later adaptive threshold / ensemble / fake GPIO) runs on MVTec texture categories with measurable FP rate. Target after adaptive threshold: FP < 5%.

## Coding conventions
- Prefer clear scripts under `scripts/` and reusable logic under `src/kumasgoz/`.
- Do not re-download MVTec if local archive / `data/mvtec` exists.
- Keep hardware/GPIO behind interfaces so fake GPIO can swap to real GPIO later.
- Do not commit `data/`, `results/`, checkpoints, or secrets.
